    "body": "## Purpose\n\nFollow-up to #57092, per @AndreasKaratzas's review question there.\n\n`test_online_fp8_moe_logprobs_bitwise_bs1_vs_bsN` was gated with `@skip_if_not_cuda`. That marker was copied from the neighboring test, not chosen because of a known ROCm limitation; the fix in #57092 was only validated on CUDA (sm_120 locally, sm_90 by a third party).\n\nThis PR switches the test to `@skip_if_not_cuda_alike` so the AMD batch-invariance jobs (which already run the whole `v1/determinism/test_batch_invariance.py`) exercise it too. On ROCm it additionally requires capability 9.4+ (MI300/MI355): gfx90a (MI250) reports 9.0 and would otherwise pass the CUDA `SM 8.9` check despite having no FP8.\n\nOpen question for ROCm owners: I could not check which MoE experts online `fp8_per_tensor` selects on ROCm (e.g. AITER vs Triton). If that path is not batch-invariant yet, this test will fail on MI300/MI355 and we'll know the ROCm path still needs the per-token activation treatment from #57092.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `pytest tests/v1/determinism/test_batch_invariance.py::test_online_fp8_moe_logprobs_bitwise_bs1_vs_bsN` on RTX 5090 (sm_120)\n- ROCm coverage via the MI300 / MI355 batch-invariance Buildkite jobs (no AMD hardware locally)\n\n## Test Result\n\n- CUDA (sm_120): 1 passed, unchanged from before.\n- ROCm: pending CI.\n\n---\n\nAI assistance was used to prepare this change; I reviewed every line and ran the test above.\n",
